@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-interpretation-time`

-- Tests of usca-interpretation-time.l4.  Each expected value is decided from the section cited in the comment above the
-- assertion, or from an independent Python script written from the statute text, which steps forward day by day on Python's own calendar
-- (it is not part of this row), never from the module.  A failing assertion is a finding.
-- Calendars supplied by this file.  The module hard-codes none.

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`366 holidays in a row from 14 March 2026` d MEANS d AT LEAST YMD 2026 3 14 AND d AT MOST YMD 2027 3 14

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`367 holidays in a row from 14 March 2026` d MEANS d AT LEAST YMD 2026 3 14 AND d AT MOST YMD 2027 3 15

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sundays only` d MEANS `is a Sunday` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays and Sundays` d MEANS `is a Saturday` d OR `is a Sunday` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays, Sundays and Monday 16 March 2026` d MEANS `is a Saturday` d OR `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 16

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sundays and Wednesday 6 May 2026` d MEANS `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 5 6

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every day is a holiday` d MEANS TRUE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no day is a holiday` d MEANS FALSE


§ `Weekdays (daydate's Weekday of: 0 is Sunday)`

-- Calendar facts, checked against an independent script: 1 February 2026 is a Sunday, so 31 January 2026 is a Saturday.
#ASSERT `is a Sunday` (YMD 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Saturday` (YMD 2026 2 1))
#ASSERT `is a Saturday` (YMD 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Sunday` (YMD 2026 1 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Sunday` (YMD 2026 2 2))
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Saturday` (YMD 2026 2 2))
#ASSERT `is a Sunday` (YMD 2030 9 1)
#ASSERT `is a Sunday` (YMD 2028 7 16)

§ `Gov. Code § 6802: which years are leap years`

-- § 6802: 1900, 2100, 2200, 2300 and any other future hundredth year are common years, except every fourth hundredth year: 2000, 2400, 2800.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 1900)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2100)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2200)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2300)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2500)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 3000)
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2000
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2400
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2800
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 3200
-- Every fourth year not a hundredth is a leap year.
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 1904
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2004
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2024
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2028
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2096
#ASSERT `is a leap year under section 6802` 2104
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 1901)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 1999)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2001)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2101)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2099)
-- The text names no rule for a hundredth year before 1900: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `is a leap year under section 6802` 1800 BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6802 names 1900 and later hundredth years, and says every fourth year is a leap year by usage; for an earlier hundredth year it does not say whether the Gregorian exception of § 6801 applies"
#ASSERT REFUSED `is a leap year under section 6802` 1700 BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6802 names 1900 and later hundredth years, and says every fourth year is a leap year by usage; for an earlier hundredth year it does not say whether the Gregorian exception of § 6801 applies"
#ASSERT REFUSED `is a leap year under section 6802` 1600 BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6802 names 1900 and later hundredth years, and says every fourth year is a leap year by usage; for an earlier hundredth year it does not say whether the Gregorian exception of § 6801 applies"
-- Agreement with daydate's Gregorian calendar for the years in the worked cases (a cross-check, not the source of any value).
#ASSERT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2024) EQUALS (`Days in month` 2 2024 EQUALS 29)
#ASSERT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2025) EQUALS (`Days in month` 2 2025 EQUALS 29)
#ASSERT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2028) EQUALS (`Days in month` 2 2028 EQUALS 29)
#ASSERT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2030) EQUALS (`Days in month` 2 2030 EQUALS 29)
#ASSERT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2100) EQUALS (`Days in month` 2 2100 EQUALS 29)
#ASSERT (`is a leap year under section 6802` 2000) EQUALS (`Days in month` 2 2000 EQUALS 29)

§ `Gov. Code § 6800: periods of days, first day excluded and last day included`

-- § 6800: the time is computed by excluding the first day and including the last, so n days from a day end n days later.
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 11)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 30 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 365 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 366 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 2 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 3 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 13) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 16)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 60 `days counted from` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 13)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 7 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 17)
-- A period of days is not a § 6803 year: 366 days from 1 January 2024 is 1 January 2025, with no pairing of 28 and 29 February.
-- Not whole days: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 0 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6800 counts whole days, excluding the first and including the last, so a period of no days or of part of a day has no last day in the text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` -1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6800 counts whole days, excluding the first and including the last, so a period of no days or of part of a day has no last day in the text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1.5 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6800 counts whole days, excluding the first and including the last, so a period of no days or of part of a day has no last day in the text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 0.5 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6800 counts whole days, excluding the first and including the last, so a period of no days or of part of a day has no last day in the text"

§ `Gov. Code § 6805: a week is seven consecutive days`

#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 17)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 2 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 52 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 6)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 3 8) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 4 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 2 3) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 3)
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 0 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6805 says a week consists of seven consecutive days; the text does not count part of a week"
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` -2 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6805 says a week consists of seven consecutive days; the text does not count part of a week"
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1.5 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6805 says a week consists of seven consecutive days; the text does not count part of a week"
#ASSERT `days in a week under section 6805` EQUALS 7

§ `Gov. Code § 6804, § 6800: periods of months`

-- A month is a calendar month (§ 6804); the first day is excluded and the last included (§ 6800).  Read as arriving at the day with
-- the same number n calendar months on (fork F-month).  Where that month has no such day the text does not say: refused.
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS (YMD 2025 2 15)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 12 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 12 15)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 3 `months counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 10)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 2 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS (YMD 2025 3 31)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2024 1 29) EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 4 30) EQUALS (YMD 2025 5 30)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 29)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 48 `months counted from` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS (YMD 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 13 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 15)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 28)
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 2 `months counted from` (YMD 2026 12 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the start day's number: Gov. Code § 6804 says only that a month is a calendar month and § 6800 excludes the first day and includes the last, so the text does not say what the last day is (daydate's add months would give the last day of the month, Date would roll into the next month, and the text licenses neither)"
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 7 31) EQUALS (YMD 2025 8 31)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 5 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 7 31) EQUALS (YMD 2025 12 31)
