#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 5 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the start day's number: Gov. Code § 6804 says only that a month is a calendar month and § 6800 excludes the first day and includes the last, so the text does not say what the last day is (daydate's add months would give the last day of the month, Date would roll into the next month, and the text licenses neither)"
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 3 30) EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 30)
#ASSERT REFUSED `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 3 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 11 30) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the start day's number: Gov. Code § 6804 says only that a month is a calendar month and § 6800 excludes the first day and includes the last, so the text does not say what the last day is (daydate's add months would give the last day of the month, Date would roll into the next month, and the text licenses neither)"
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 3 29) EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 29)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2024 3 29) EQUALS (YMD 2024 4 29)
