§ `Gov. Code § 6803: year, half year and quarter of a year`

-- § 6803: a year is 365 days, a half year 182, a quarter of a year 91; the added day of a leap year and the day immediately
-- preceding it, if they occur in the period, are reckoned together as one day.
#ASSERT `days in a year under section 6803` EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `days in a half year under section 6803` EQUALS 182
#ASSERT `days in a quarter of a year under section 6803` EQUALS 91
-- No leap day in the period: plain 365, 182, 91 days.
-- Worked cases of the brief.
-- Leap day inside the period: the pair counts once, so the last day is one calendar day later than 365 n days on.
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `years counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `years counted from` (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 2 `years counted from` (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `half years counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 7 2)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 1 `quarters of a year counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 2)
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of` 2 `quarters of a year counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 7 2)
