-- A calendar with no free day within 366 days is refused rather than looped over.
#ASSERT REFUSED `extended to the next day that is not a holiday` `every day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 14) BECAUSE "the calendar supplied makes more than 366 consecutive days holidays, so there is no next day that is not a holiday to extend to"
-- The loop guard is not a rule of the text: it is a limit on the calendar a caller may supply.  366 holidays in a row from 14 March 2026 (through 14 March 2027) still resolve, to 15 March 2027; 367 in a row are refused.
#ASSERT `extended to the next day that is not a holiday` `366 holidays in a row from 14 March 2026` (YMD 2026 3 14) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 15)
