#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 10 days `counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 20)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 days `counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `under the calendar` `Saturdays and Sundays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 11)
-- A last day refused by the month rule stays refused through the calendar.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 months `counted from` (YMD 2025 1 31) `under the calendar` `Sundays only` BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the start day's number: Gov. Code § 6804 says only that a month is a calendar month and § 6800 excludes the first day and includes the last, so the text does not say what the last day is (daydate's add months would give the last day of the month, Date would roll into the next month, and the text licenses neither)"
-- Intermediate holidays do not move the last day: 3 days from Friday 13 March 2026 under 'Saturdays and Sundays' counts Saturday and Sunday and ends Monday 16 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 days `counted from` (YMD 2026 3 13) `under the calendar` `Saturdays and Sundays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 16)
-- Two days from Friday 13 March end on Sunday 15 March, which is extended to Monday 16 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 days `counted from` (YMD 2026 3 13) `under the calendar` `Saturdays and Sundays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 16)

