§ `The helpers of the § 6803 count, directly`

-- A whole number of at least one: the text counts whole periods.
#ASSERT `n is a whole number of at least one` 1
#ASSERT `n is a whole number of at least one` 2
#ASSERT `n is a whole number of at least one` 3
#ASSERT `n is a whole number of at least one` 12
#ASSERT `n is a whole number of at least one` 100
#ASSERT `n is a whole number of at least one` 365
#ASSERT NOT (`n is a whole number of at least one` 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`n is a whole number of at least one` -1)
#ASSERT NOT (`n is a whole number of at least one` -100)
#ASSERT NOT (`n is a whole number of at least one` 0.5)
#ASSERT NOT (`n is a whole number of at least one` 1.5)
#ASSERT NOT (`n is a whole number of at least one` 2.25)
-- Whether the leap-day pair lies in a period: the added day (29 February) and the day immediately preceding it (28 February) must both occur in the period.
#ASSERT `leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 12 31) 2024 FALSE
#ASSERT `leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 12 31) 2024 TRUE
-- 28 February is the excluded first day: no pair on the literal reading, a pair on the purposive reading.
#ASSERT NOT (`leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2024 12 31) 2024 FALSE)
#ASSERT `leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2024 12 31) 2024 TRUE
-- The period ends on 28 February: the added day is not in it.
#ASSERT NOT (`leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 2 27) (YMD 2024 2 28) 2024 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 2 27) (YMD 2024 2 28) 2024 TRUE)
#ASSERT `leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 2 27) (YMD 2024 2 29) 2024 FALSE
-- The first day is 29 February itself: its 28 February is before the period on either reading.
#ASSERT NOT (`leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 12 31) 2024 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 12 31) 2024 TRUE)
-- A common year, and 2100, which § 6802 makes a common year.
#ASSERT NOT (`leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) 2025 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2100 1 1) (YMD 2100 12 31) 2100 FALSE)
#ASSERT `leap-day pair of the year lies in the period` (YMD 2000 1 1) (YMD 2000 12 31) 2000 FALSE
-- The pairs in a run of years: 2024 and 2028 in 1 March 2023 to 31 December 2028; none after the last year.
#ASSERT `count of leap-day pairs in the period` (YMD 2023 3 1) (YMD 2028 12 31) 2023 2028 FALSE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `count of leap-day pairs in the period` (YMD 2023 3 1) (YMD 2028 12 31) 2025 2027 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `count of leap-day pairs in the period` (YMD 2023 3 1) (YMD 2028 12 31) 2029 2028 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `count of leap-day pairs in the period` (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2028 2 29) 2024 2028 FALSE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `count of leap-day pairs in the period` (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2028 2 29) 2024 2028 TRUE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `count of leap-day pairs in the period` (YMD 2096 1 1) (YMD 2104 12 31) 2096 2104 FALSE EQUALS 2
-- 2096, 2104 are leap years and 2100 is not: two pairs in 1 January 2096 to 31 December 2104.
-- The end day number: first day's number plus the length plus the pairs found.  One year from 1 March 2023 ends on 1 March 2024 (366 calendar days on, the pair once).
#ASSERT `day number on which a count of units ends` (YMD 2023 3 1) 365 FALSE (Day (YMD 2023 3 1) PLUS 365) EQUALS Day (YMD 2024 3 1)
#ASSERT `day number on which a count of units ends` (YMD 2025 7 16) 1095 FALSE (Day (YMD 2025 7 16) PLUS 1095) EQUALS Day (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT `day number on which a count of units ends` (YMD 2025 7 16) 1095 FALSE (Day (YMD 2028 7 16)) EQUALS Day (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT `last day of a count of units in which the leap-day pair counts once` 1095 (YMD 2025 7 16) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT `last day of a count of units in which the leap-day pair counts once` 730 (YMD 2024 2 28) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 27)
#ASSERT `last day of a count of units in which the leap-day pair counts once` 730 (YMD 2024 2 28) TRUE EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `last day of a count of units in which the leap-day pair counts once` 1 (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 11)
#ASSERT `last day of n periods of fixed length` 3 365 (YMD 2025 7 16) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT `last day of n periods of fixed length` 2 91 (YMD 2023 12 1) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2024 6 1)
#ASSERT `last day of n periods of fixed length` 1 7 (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 17)
#ASSERT REFUSED `last day of n periods of fixed length` 0 365 (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6803 defines year, half year and quarter of a year as whole lengths; the text does not count part of one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `last day of n periods of fixed length` 1.5 365 (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6803 defines year, half year and quarter of a year as whole lengths; the text does not count part of one"
#ASSERT `next day from the date that is not a holiday, counting days so far` `Sundays only` (YMD 2026 3 15) 0 EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 16)
#ASSERT `next day from the date that is not a holiday, counting days so far` `Sundays only` (YMD 2026 3 16) 0 EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 16)
#ASSERT `next day from the date that is not a holiday, counting days so far` `Saturdays and Sundays` (YMD 2026 3 14) 0 EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 16)
#ASSERT REFUSED `next day from the date that is not a holiday, counting days so far` `Sundays only` (YMD 2026 3 15) 366 BECAUSE "the calendar supplied makes more than 366 consecutive days holidays, so there is no next day that is not a holiday to extend to"
#ASSERT `next day from the date that is not a holiday, counting days so far` `Sundays only` (YMD 2026 3 16) 366 EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 16)
